<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argentina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Argentina is a country in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> that emerged from the Spanish viceroyalty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>. In the nineteenth century it was a rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> for influence in the Río de la Plata region, notably in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war">Cisplatine War</a>, and later an ally in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguayan-war">Paraguayan War</a>. Its economy was closely tied to British investment and trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argentina.jpg" alt="Argentina" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manuel Belgrano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Argentina.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
